From: OpenATV <info@opena.tv>
Subject: [PATCH] avrcp: restore address input names for legacy libreader

The proprietary SF8008 and GB Trio 4K Pro libreader versions read virtual
input device names and use them as Bluetooth addresses in bluetoothctl
queries and the BlueALSA PCM configuration. The human-readable name with
an AVRCP suffix is not an address, so connected headsets are no longer
selected as audio outputs.

Restore the remote address as the AVRCP input device name for these receivers.
Keep the actual device name for the existing key quirks, and preserve the
adapter address, input identity and key handling used by bt_uinput.

This is a receiver compatibility workaround, not a general BlueZ change.
The build recipe applies it only to SF8008 and GB Trio 4K Pro, whose
libreader versions require the legacy naming convention.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [compatibility with proprietary libreader]
Bug: https://github.com/openatv/enigma2/issues/4086
---
 profiles/audio/avctp.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/profiles/audio/avctp.c b/profiles/audio/avctp.c
--- a/profiles/audio/avctp.c
+++ b/profiles/audio/avctp.c
@@ -1140,6 +1140,7 @@ static void init_uinput(struct avctp *session)
 {
 	struct btd_adapter *adapter = device_get_adapter(session->device);
 	char name[UINPUT_MAX_NAME_SIZE];
+	char address[18];
 	struct input_id id;
 	int err;
 
@@ -1156,7 +1157,8 @@ static void init_uinput(struct avctp *session)
 	id.product = btd_device_get_product(session->device);
 	id.version = btd_device_get_version(session->device);
 
-	session->uinput = bt_uinput_new(name, " (AVRCP)",
+	ba2str(device_get_address(session->device), address);
+	session->uinput = bt_uinput_new(address, NULL,
 				btd_adapter_get_address(adapter), &id);
 	bt_uinput_set_debug(session->uinput, uinput_debug, NULL);
 
